namespace trion:
    use formal
    use software

    section "Two levels of proof":
        The metatheoretic proof means the proof about the trion language.
        A result proof means the proof that certifies exactly one verification result.
        The trustworthiness of the trion language rests on the metatheoretic proof and on the result proofs.

    section "The metatheoretic proof":
        The logical vocabulary means the words of the trion language that join formulas.
        The resolution calculus means the calculus that resolves a set of contracts with the inference rules of the logical vocabulary.

        [PROOF-RULES-CONSISTENT]
        The inference rules of the logical vocabulary shall be mutually consistent.

        The resolution calculus has soundness, refutational completeness, termination, and confluence.

        [PROOF-SOUND]
        The metatheoretic proof shall establish the soundness of the resolution calculus.

        [PROOF-COMPLETE]
        The metatheoretic proof shall establish the refutational completeness of the resolution calculus.

        [PROOF-TERMINATING]
        The metatheoretic proof shall establish the termination of the resolution calculus.

        [PROOF-CONFLUENT]
        The metatheoretic proof shall establish the confluence of the resolution calculus.

        [PROOF-NOT-SELF-VERIFICATION]
        The trion processor shall not accept a verification result as the metatheoretic proof.

    section "The proof of a verification result":
        An external proof checker means a proof checker that is independent of the trion processor.
        The surface text means the text of a specification that an author wrote.
        An expansion rule means a rule that expands a composition.
        A reading rule means a rule that reads a short sentence as a contract.
        A language rule means an expansion rule, a reading rule, or an inference rule of the logical vocabulary.
        Each result proof has one or more steps.

        [PROOF-EXTERNAL]
        An external proof checker shall check each result proof.

        [PROOF-FROM-TEXT]
        Each result proof shall start from the surface text of the specification.

        [PROOF-EVERY-STEP]
        The external proof checker shall check each step of a result proof against the language rules.

    section "What is trusted":
        The trusted base means the set of things that a person trusts for a verification result.
        The trusted base has one or more members.

        [PROOF-NO-DISCRETION]
        The language rules shall determine the contracts of each surface text.

        Each surface text has one or more contracts.

        [PROOF-REJECT-FOREIGN]
        If a formula of a result proof does not follow from the surface text, then the external proof checker shall reject the result proof.

        [PROOF-TRUSTED-BASE]
        Each member of the trusted base shall be a language rule or the external proof checker.

    section "An external prover decides each query again":
        A query means a formula set that the trion processor decides for a verification result.
        The external prover means a program outside the trion processor that decides a query.

        [PROVER-ASKED]
        The trion processor shall send each query of a verification result to the external prover.

        [PROVER-DIFFERENCE]
        If the answer of the external prover differs from the answer of the trion processor, then the trion processor shall report an error.

        [PROVER-OPEN]
        If the external prover gives no answer to a query, then the trion processor shall report an error.
